    {
      "title": "Wedgewood Partners Third Quarter 2025 Client Letter",
      "fund": "Wedgewood Partners",
      "date": "Q3 2025",
      "summary": "Wedgewood Partners evaluates Copart's stock underperformance driven by market fears over near-term U.S. salvage unit volume loss to primary competitor RB Global (IAA) at Progressive Corp. Wedgewood argues the sell-off is overly pessimistic, noting that Copart grew gross profit dollars by 12% and EPS by 24%, while holding ~$5 billion in net cash. They expect volume share to normalize over time as Copart's superior auction buyer density and liquidity remain unmatched in the marketplace.",
      "url": "https://substack.com/search/CPRT%20Copart%2C%20Inc.%20investment%20thesis",
      "btn_label": "Substack Search \u2197"
    },
    {
      "title": "Copart ($CPRT) Deep Dive",
      "fund": "Substack / Margin Valley Research",
      "date": "May 23, 2026",
      "summary": "Margin Valley Research conducts an operational and financial teardown of Copart, focusing on its high-ROIC operating model and non-discretionary inventory flow from insurance carriers. The memo details how structural inflation in vehicle technology and repair costs incentives insurers to declare total losses, feeding Copart's capital-light auction platform. Unit economics benefit from incremental fee capture on international buyers and power sports expansions, making the company's high operating margins resilient through economic cycles.",
